  "stem": "advanced_shipping_2023_W13_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-13",
  "source_file": "advanced_shipping_2023_W13_ADVANCED-MARKET-REPORT-WEEK-13.pdf",
  "issue_date": "2023-03-31",
  "report_week": "13",
  "report_period": "Week 13 (24th Mar to 31st Mar 2023)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Following the sale of the Capesize \"C H S Creation\" 174/2006 SWS, China (SS 03/2026, DD 03/2024, BWTS fitted) at USD 17 mill, Mssrs COSCO HK Shipping have now committed the Japanese built \"C H S Splendor\" 170/2006 IHI, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 02/2024, BWTS fitted) to Middle Eastern buyers for mid-high USD 17 mill. Uglands Rederi have sold their Supramax \"Carmencita\" 58/2009 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS/DD 05/2024, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed buyers for USD 16 mill, while the two-years-older sister vessel \"Iris Express\" 58/2007 Tsuneishi Cebu, Philippines (SS 03/2027, DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold a week ago at USD 14,4 mill. In addition, Hsin Chien Marine sold their \"New Beginning\" 56/2013 Mitsui, Japan (SS 01/2028, DD 02/2026, BWTS fitted) to Greek buyers for USD 20,5 mill. JP Morgan have acquired three Handysize vessels from Swire Shipping, the \"Erisort\" 39/2014 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 10/2024, BWTS fiited), the sister vessel \"Erradale\" 39/2014 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 08/2024, BWTS fitted) and the \"Wulin\" 39/2014 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 03/2024, BWTS fitted) for low- mid USD 20 mill each. Remind you that earlier this month, the one-year- younger \"Cielo Di Angra\"39/2015 Yangfan, China (SS 10/2025, DD 09/2023, BWTS fitted) & \"Cielo Di Valparaiso\" 39/2015 Yangfan, China (SS 06/2025, DD 07/2023, BWTS fitted) were sold at USD 20 mill each.",
    "tankers": "BW Group have sold their LR1 sister vessels \"Hafnia Hudson\" 76/2007 Dalian, China (SS 06/2027, DD 07/2025, BWTS fitted) & \"Hafnia Danube\" 76/2007 Dalian, China (SS 03/2027, DD 06/2025, BWTS fitted) for excess USD 23 mill each. Note that back in February, the \"Hafnia Columbia\" 76/2007 Dalian, China (SS 01/2027, DD 03/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold at high USD 22 mill. The MR2 \"PTI Danube\" 50/2017 Spp, Korea (SS 01/2027, DD 02/2025, BWTS fitted) was committed for excess USD 40 mill basis delivery July 2023. Moreover, Nyhill Shipping & Trading sold their \"Jo Kari\" 47/2007 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 10/2026, DD 10/2024, BWTS fitted) to Turkish buyers for excess USD 22 mill. For comparison, the \"Atlantica Bay\" 46/2007 Sungdong, Korea (SS 07/2027, DD 10/2025, BWTS fitted) was sold earlier this month at USD 21,8 mill. Ancora Investment Trust have committed their MR1 \"Jemma\" 38/2008 Guangzhou, China (SS/DD 06/2023) to Turkish buyers for USD 18 mill. For reference, the one-year-older sister vessel \"Nordic Tatiana\" 38/2007 Guangzhou, China (SS 09/2027, DD 10/2025) was sold back in January at USD 16 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of high usd 7,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 12,000/14,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 12,000/14,000 pd range. A number of Australian trips into India were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. Indian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. West African trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 22,000/23,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 18,000/20,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 16,500/18,500 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 650K/850K. A Kamsarmax was fixed on period at the usd 17,000 pd basis delivery China for 1 year employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of trips from China into Singapore with aggregates were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed at the usd 11,000/13,000 pd range. A number of Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/15,000 pd. South African trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 15,000/17,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "A generally quiet week for this segment. Inter-Mediterranean trips were reported at the level of usd 13,000/14,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via Black Sea into US Gulf with minerals were fixed around usd 10,000/13,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
